Once the reduction is gone the rate falls to 28.6% from $21,177. It steps up to 34.7% from $31,273 (the second bracket) and 41.2% from $59,079 (the federal 20.5% bracket), then down as pension and insurance stop. The top rate in this chart is 54%, from $259,609, where the line is straight."
